<title>USA: IBM unit files $3.5 bln debt shelf offering.</title>
<headline>IBM unit files $3.5 bln debt shelf offering.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>IBM Credit Corp, a financing unit of International Business Machines Corp, filed Wednesday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission a shelf offering of up to $3.5 billion in debt securities.</p>
<p>Together with previous registrations, the shelf offering totals $3.984 billion.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale will be used for general corporate purposes. No underwriters were named in the shelf offering.</p>
</text>
